  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 223 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nMid-level troughing between ridging east and west of the area will \nremain over the area through the weekend. For now, the trough will \nremain located generally over the water, and will keep the best rain \nchances there and up into the Victoria Crossroads region. We will \nsee a general lowering of deep moisture tomorrow from levels that \nare currently well above normal (2.1-2.25\"). The pocket of highest \nmoisture will drift northeastward, but remain close enough to keep \nmoderate rain chances in the Victoria Crossroads. Elsewhere, \nsufficient moisture will still be in play for isolated sea breeze \nshowers daily. By Sunday the trough begins to move westward while \nalso starting to weaken. As it does move westward though it could \nprovide a bit higher rain chances, mainly for the Coastal Plains. \nMonday through much of next week return to being dominated by high \npressure which means limited rain chances.\n\nTemperatures remain above normal daily through the period with highs \nfrom the lower to mid 90s along the coast to around 105 in the Brush \nCountry. These values are 5 to 10 degrees above normal for this time \nof year. Heat index values will also be high with a few locations \npotentially toping 110 daily. The highest heat index values are \nexpected Friday and Saturday and a heat advisory may be warranted \none or both of those days.",
